id: pm-package-grammar24
title: Align the host grammar census with the latest installed package command
description: "Installing the latest supported pm-changelog2026.10.24 correctly exposes changelog contracts, but pm-cli's SDK-owned package destination census omits it. The live command-grammar gate fails with missing_destination and stale_observed_signature. This is host contract inventory drift, not a changelog generator defect; preserve package ownership and the existing noun/verb surface."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[3]: contracts,packages,sdk
created_at: "2026-10-24T10:17:55.861Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-24T10:22:42.373Z"
assignee: "harness:codex"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#67ddd7c5bf7e85e8f28aa1ff"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 45
acceptance_criteria: "Declare the new command as package-owned in the SDK census; Preserve its empty positional shape and validate live structured help; Pass command grammar, generated contracts and public SDK surface gates without weakening them"
parent: pm-1kxs
risk: low
confidence: 90
expected_result: The latest installed package remains executable and its command is accounted for by host grammar and positional contracts.
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-24T10:17:55.861Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: fresh exact changelog contracts search and current open/in_progress lists plus the all-status strict corpus found no integration owner for the new package command. Reuse the live agent grammar parent; the prior closed census owner remains completed. Before-fix full static gate captures missing_destination and stale_observed_signature for the package's real newly installed command. Package-owned changelog generate/check both pass, so generator implementation stays upstream and unchanged."
  "2026-10-24T10:20:22.962Z","harness:codex","Implemented the host integration using the existing package-owned destination table, retaining the package identity and empty positional slots. Extended the existing published-package contract table test rather than duplicating a fixture or changing generator implementation. Both focused grammar suites pass37 cases. The expected SDK contract snapshot drift is generated with contracts:update; the live grammar census and strict full static gates remain required, with no waived unknown command or positional checks."
